Anything other than standard 'make config' is haphazard.  From my
experience, I can do a 'make xconfig' on a pristine kernel+patches, but
after that, the only thing that works reliably is 'make config'.

> MILO loads and unzips the file, but as soon as I get the "jumping to the
> kernel" message, and the dashed line across the screen, nothing happens.
> My (admittedly novice) opinion is that something is wrong with the
> executable format of the vmlinux.gz file. 

Did you get the right one?  Alpha kernels live in arch/alpha/boot/ - I
don't think a 'make install' works right.  Best to manually cp the file
into your root directory.

> Is there something simple I'm missing?

That should be it.  Once you get past the MILO stuff, it's pretty easy.

