There are calls to iopl (or was it ioperm?) that don't work on
the Alpha, but that aren't neccesary either. Simply comment them out,
or, like Michael suggested, grep an updated package.

> I gave up on isapnptools.  The card I have is a SoundBlaster 16 Value
> (which I beleive is PnP). I put it in an x86 PC, got the creative labs config

I got a SB 16 PnP Value - Waveplay working in my Alpha, one equiped
with the Vibra Chip. That one lacks an 16 bit DMA channel, so I
had to treat it like an 8 bit card in the setup of the sound driver.

Setting up Pnp was quite easy. You use pnpdump to see what the
card supports, and edit the output to use it as input for isapnp.
Of course this is not really PnP as you have to choose the right
IRQs and such by yourself, and you got to make sure that your
not conflicting with the automated PCI stuff. A problem I don't got
with my EISA machine :-)

I succesfully used the card with kernels 2.0.30 and 2.1.89.

Martin
