> Hello all!  I know this is off-topic, but I am getting desperate.  I have 
> some binary files that were generated on an sgi, but I need to read them 
> on my Alpha (UDB with linux 2.0.20).  I have learned that the sgi is 
> big-endian, where the alpha is little-endian.  The files are in the 
> following format:
> 
> 1 int followed by 52 doubles - repeated 20,000 times.

Is this an unformatted fortran file? In which case, the format is:

record length
data
repeat record length

On the SGI and Digital Unix, the record length is a 32 bit int. On the
latest f2c libraries, it's 64 bits. You have to account for this.

-- g


