Ints(32bit) should be swaped 

1,2,3,4 => 4,3,2,1 in 4 byte chunks

If I remember correctly ieee is defined in a endian insensitive format. 
That is you should be able to read it correctly on all machines. But it 
has been a long time and I may have forgotten somthing.
If the doubles have to be swaped you should be swaping the order

1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8 => 8,7,6,5,4,3,2,1 in 8 byte chunks

