It depends when they are coming from.  If they are from the current g77
then f2c.h defines there, correctly I would argue, Fortran 'integer'
type as 'int' - i.e. 32 bits.

One has to be careful with that.  An unfortunate result of living on a
"bleeding edge".  Defining 'integer' as 'long' in headers which came with
'f2c' tranlator is a bug resulting likely from an attempt to acommodate
MS-DOS machines.

I would do such conversion in question in Perl anyway. You are working
too hard if you attempt to use anything else for the task. :-)

