> > On the
> > latest f2c libraries, it's 64 bits. You have to account for this.
> 
> It depends when they are coming from.  If they are from the current g77
> then f2c.h defines there, correctly I would argue, Fortran 'integer'
> type as 'int' - i.e. 32 bits.

The size of a Fortran integer is different from the size of the
Fortran record length. The latest g77 for alphas (egcs) has
these as 32 and 64 bits, respectively.

I think the record length size should be settable per-file at runtime,
but no one's done that yet.

-- g


