I have used a version of 3c509.c for Linux that could change the values.
Unfortunately it's timing got all screwed up on the alpha, and the entire
NVRAM was filled with zeros. So I had to reprogram all values by hand
(including mac address), since I naturally didn't make a backup of the
NVRAM before I started (no, I don't like rm -i either :).

Therefore, unless you are certain you have a working version or know what 
you are doing, don't try this at home, kids!

/Andreas


