I managed to get my Soundblaster AWE64 properly initialized and recognized
by a 2.1.88 kernel with Tom Lees's PnP patches. No big deal, but:

(A) it works on alpha, which may be good news for those on axp-list who had
problems with the isapnptools. (I had reported before (on pnp-users) that I
could compile a bootable kernel. This time I actually moved the card and
checked that it worked.)

(B) though the docs state otherwise, it works with SMP. Needs just one
small change in init/main.c (around line 1070 (IIRC), change the order of
smp_init and pnp_init)
(SMP/intel that is. I guess Jay's about the only one who can check it for
SMP/alpha.)


things left to do:
- try the 2.0.33 version
- make non-module soundblaster drivers pnp-aware
- make this stuff part of standard kernel (2.2.x?)


