On Sun, 5 Apr 1998, Alvin Starr wrote:

> Does anybody know of an mp3 encoder for linux-alpha?

Well, I have been optimizing the reference code a little (the original is
about 4.5 times slower than my current version on my 164SX). My 164SX
encodes mp3:s 2.5 times faster than a PPro 200 with the same source and it
takes ~40 seconds to encode 30 seconds of music with my machine.

It encodes the file file.wav to file.mp3 with these switches:

encode -l 3 -p 2 -m s -b 128 file.wav file.mp3

Unfortunately there is no support for joint-stereo in layer 3, so you'll
have to settle for stereo-mode.

BTW: If anyone knows how to do joint-stereo in layer 3, I'm interrested..

Ok, it's at my ftp:

ftp://wopr.campus.luth.se/pub/encoder.tgz

/Andreas


