Jason L. Prigge wrote:
> 
> I just recently installed RedHat for Alpha and wish to install Oracle SQL*Net V2
> from the Oracle for Dec Unix CD-ROM.  The CD is not ISO-9660 compliant and errors out when I try and mount it.  Is there a utility for this somewhere?


If the CD is UFS there is read-only support for this file system
available. You may have to re-compile your kernel to enable this
capability.

If the block size is 512k you may have to use a CD drive that supports
this. Most CD drives sold for PCs and MACs support only the 2048 block
size. Drives referred to as "Sun Bootable" support 512k blocks.

I have no idea whether the program you are trying to install will run
under Linux/Alpha. Even if it does you may need some of the DU libraries
and that requires a DU  license.

-- 
Brian E.W. Wood  beww@intac.com


