Hi !

> I have tried similar, and find that (so far) quick attempts at mounting
> this UFS are not easily accomplished. However I can say that it seems to
> use regular 2048K blocks.

2048K ;-}

Be careful. There is a big difference between physical sector size for data
tracks (fixed 2048); the logical SCSI-transfer length (256,512,1024,2048) 
for a logical data block; and the block size of the filesystem.

DU requires that the CD-ROM drives uses 512 Bytes/logical block and some
drives won't do that. Linux supports 2048 and 512 operations. 

But what if SCSI-transfer length is 2048; and a fancy filesystem requires
512/Bytes Block ? 
Look into sr.c and you know that it works.

