On Tue, 7 Apr 1998, -Matt Good- wrote:

> Can anyone elighten me on what I need to do to fix this problem.
> I don't get any errors prior to this. I am using Redhat 5.0, with all of
> the updated rpms installed. 
> I have gotten the same errors with binutiles 2.8.1.0.29 and 2.8.1.0.1. 

(snip) 
 
> arch/alpha/kernel/kernel.o: In function `do_entIF':
> traps.c(.text+0x1098): undefined reference to `alpha_fp_emul'
> traps.c(.text+0x109c): undefined reference to `alpha_fp_emul'
> make: *** [vmlinux] Error 1

I'll bet you used menuconfig or xconfig to setup features prior to
compilation, no?  Currently, neither works correctly on Alpha platforms.
Use plain, old 'make config' and be sure to answer 'Y' to the question
mentioning "Kernel FP software completion" (almost at the end).  Then do a
full "make dep; make clean; make boot" and you'll be in business.

Steve



