> 
> I don't
> think Linux can read an NTFS formatted disk - maybe I'm wrong. 

Linux can read NTFS partitions for a long, long time.  I do not think
that anybody was brave enough to try to **write** to NTFS partitions
as the whole "documentation" for this file system is based on
observations and guesses (do you still wonder why?).

It is true that NTFS support is not included in officially released
kernels so far - in a big part due to this forced "works for me" status.
I did not hear of anybody who would patch milo sources to read such
partitions.  I guess there was no big demand for that and putting your
boot image on such partition would be pretty inconvenient.  You would
