At 3:22 PM -0500 on 4/7/98, JOHN PRICE wrote:


> OK, I really meant 3.5".  I already have a 500M drive to boot from.  I
> just need some more user space.

I would recommend that you look into external SCSI drives. You'll be a lot
happier, I believe. Here's the deal:

Multia's come with a vanilla IDE controller (not EIDE or UltraIDE), which
already means a low transfer speed. Add to this the current situation where
disk operations to the IDE drive take up 100% of the CPU time, and you've
got a problem.

Plus, two internal hard drives would be a rather bad thing. Two HDs would
put out far too much heat to be safe, and would also draw too much juice
(the power supply is very puny).

> Why would there be an IDE connector if there is no cable that will
> convert from 2mm to 0.1"?

There may be, but you'll likely have some trouble finding one.

> There is nothing in the PCI slot.  I was going to not use it and have
> another hard drive.

It is possible to use a 3.5" drive if you remove the PCI riser card.

Xi



