> 
> I have two ethernet cards, and I get this message from startup:
> 
> sysctl: ip forwarding off
> 
> Sure enough, the cards don't send anything from one to the other.

From /etc/rc.d/init.d/network:

        # Turn IP forwarding on or off. We do this before bringing up the
        # interfaces to make sure we don't forward when we shouldn't, and
        # we do it even if networking isn't configured (why not?).

and a bit later:

        echo "$value" > /proc/sys/net/ipv4/ip_forward

where $value depends on how $FORWARD_IPV4 was set in
/etc/sysconfig/network ($value is 0 or 1 - to be precise).

From what I know installation screens allow you to pick what you
want for FORWARD_IPV4, but nothing prevents you from editing
/etc/sysconfig/network manually later.

   Michal


