Not sure about a summary, but I was having problems with my UDB
spontaneously rebooting, not coming up, etc. I noticed the tarnishing around
the power connector (really only the first two pins) and was able to wiggle
the connector to either reset the system and/or let it come up. I tried
using alcohol with a cotton swab but it really wasn't dirty, it was
corroded. I then used Tarn-X on a cotton swab followed by dry wipe and
alcohol (to get rid of residual acid from Tarn-X). Since then I haven't had
any reboots or failures to come up. Cheap fix but I suspect I'll have to do
it again in another six months.

mjl


