Regarding my previous post on this subject:

A little loop over a file creation shows, that in Digital
Unix (actually, OSF/1 3.2c), the max number of open files
per process is 4096.  So I guess one should increase the
limits in include/linux/fs.h and include/linux/limits.h
by a factor of 16 if one wants to be sure that the same
code that runs under DU doesn't crash in axp-linux (now
of course if people would close their files properly...)

Marc Nicklaus


