> >"no_pci_disconnect" on the S3 boards but it works only in a number
> >9 board (S3Trio64 based). 
> 
> PowerStorm is only supported under Digital UNIX and Windows NT.

Clarification:

	3D10		S3 Trio64 of some flavor, WILL WORK with XFree86
	3D30		TGA2 8-plane 2Mb memory, no LINUX support
	4D20		TGA2 24-plane 8Mb or more, no LINUX support
	4D30/40/50/ec	Intergraph Cateyes, IIRC, no LINUX support

> That VGA chip (cirrus) still doesn't work as a X11 server.

Yes, the 3D30 and up do have some flavor of CIRRUS on them or on an attached
card, but (I thought) with relatively little VGA memory as they are only
intended to support text-mode console, not X; that's the job of the
accelerator back-end.

In addition, the CIRRUS support in XFree86 has never been ported to Alpha.

But you might be able to use the Mono server, that actually does work on most VGAs at 640x400... :-\

> The best is a Matrox Millenium, MACH64 and... (can't remeber more...)

S3, S3ViRGE, I128, P9000 are separate servers; SVGA supports Millennium
(I, and II in 3.3.2) and Mystique, S3ViRGE, and ???. Best consult the
Release Notes.

Go for a Millennium of any flavor, they have a great server...

--Jay++

