Hello;

There is a reason as to why tar and the network are linked.

The archive file may reside on another host.

Instead of having a tape drive on all my machines I have two
tape drives used by 10 machines.

Example:
tar -cvf screamer:/dev/tape -I router.files

backups all the router machine's files to the tape drive
on the 433Mhz DEC Alpha.

tar -tvf screamer:/dev/tape

lists all the files from the tape.


<Begin Quote>
Device selection and switching:
  -f, --file=[HOSTNAME:]FILE     use archive file or device FILE on HOSTNAME
      --force-local              archive file is local even if has a colon
      --rsh-command=COMMAND      use remote COMMAND instead of rsh
  -[0-7][lmh]                    specify drive and density
<End   Quote>

I have not ever noticed this problem on any of my machines.

