> typedef long int /* long int */ ftnlen;
> typedef long int /* long int */ ftnint;

Bummer!  Not again!  I actually filed a bug report, accepted, against
some snapshots between 1.0.1 and 1.0.2 because 'configure' was broken
and this 'long int' stuff showed once more and immediately created a
havoc in a library.  My temporary workaround was to add Makefile entries
which were editing automatically bad typedefs before they were used.
For reasons unclear it looks like that releases of egcs get it right
and snapshots are breaking configure script.  Mind you, snapshots are
not guaranteed to work at all and if play with they then you are
on your own and you are supposed to report bugs fast (with possible fixes).
Still I wonder why this bug shows up again, and again, and ...

