OK Guys...

Finally I got my Jensen AXP 150 Working....
I post this message here for those who have simmular problems to my
ones...

My machine is:

AXP 150 - Jensen
SCSI - Adaptec EISA 1740 (or something like this)
Floppy Controller - On the Adaptec
HD - SCSI - 532MB - Seagate
RAM - 16 MB - with Parity
Net Adapter - DE 202 - ISA
Firmware 1.7

and I got finally Red Hat 4.2 working on it...

I don't have a Red Hat CD, so I downloaded the entire RH 5.0
distribution, copied it to a local ftp server and tried to install it
via ftp... I worked on about 1 week and RH 5.0 didn't install... I tried
RH4.2 (directly from
ftp.funet.fi/pub/Linux/redhat/redhat/redhat-4.2/alpha via my provider).
I installed only the base system but I suppose the entire distribution
will work too... But I am not sure about RH 5.0 - TILL NOW IT DOESN'T
WANT TO INSTALL ON MY JENSEN... Maybe it''s my error, I will try again
when I got the CD....

So Here is what I did to get RH4.2 working on my Jensen... :

First of all I downgraded the Firmware to 1.7...  (I got it from a Linux
distribution ftp, but there are many ftps that have it...)

After downgrading the Firmware I downloaded the ARC Utils (minlabel.exe
and copyboot.exe)...

I downloaded the jensen.img (aboot + kernel 2.0.33). Note that I used
the jensen.img from the Red Hat 5.0 distribution (RH4.2 doesn't have a
jensen.img)...

After what I downloaded the ramdisk.img for Red Hat 4.2 (NOT 5.0)...

I copied the ARC Utils to a third floppy disk... (freshly formatted)...

I used dd to write the jensen.img to one and the ramdisk.img to another
floppy...
(dd if=/directory/jensen.img of`=/dev/fd0 - the same with the
ramdisk).It can be done with rawrite for DOS too....

I turned on my Jensen and I swiched to the ARC console (SET OS NT +
Powercyce in the SRM console...)

First of all I setted up my floppy drive to 2.88 (MUST BE DONE BECAUSE
copyboot.exe doesn't work propely if not configured, and the ARC console
looses config after swiching to SRM and back...)

So I ran  a:minlabel.exe....

I have a 532MB SCSI HD so I setted 3 partitions: 1 small for boot, one
for the root and one for the swap. The HD has 1 009 000 sectors or so.
My partition table looks like this:

1. /dev/sda1 - Size 10 000 sectors, filesystem 8 (ext2) offset 0
2. /dev/sda2 - Size 900 000 sectros, filesystem 8 (ext2) offset 10 001
3. /dev/sda3 - Size 90 000 sectros, filesystem 1 (swap) and offset 910
002

(IF SOMEBODY DOES MINLABEL , BE CAREFUL WITH THE OFFSET - partition 1
MUST have offset 0 for booting....)

ok... After all this write your partition table to disk and exit
minlabel.exe...
Then I run a:copyboot.exe and copied the jensen.img floppy to /dev/sda1.

Many people said me that I should copy it to /dev/sda , but after many
trys the only way I got it working was to copy jensen.img to
/dev/sda1...

After all this I swiched to the SRM console...
I typed : SET BOOT_OSFLAGS "i" to set the OS Flags.... Somebody told me
to put "INSTALL" as Boot flag, I tried and it didn't work... So I puted
"i"...

Then I typed: SET BOOTDEF_DEV DKA000 (for my only SCSI disk)... But it
should work with DKA100 200 etc. for other SCSI disks if somebody has
more than one...

then I typed: "B"... It's the same like "BOOT"....

Aboot boots and prompts me for the kernel name/arguments....
I typed:  1/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1
Other parametters like "-" didn't work by me....

The kernel booted, detected SCSI Netcard etc and prompted me for the
ramdisk...
I inserted the ramdisk.img floppy and jumped to RH Install....
I selected FTP for Installation type, but it should work by NFS or from
CD ROM/HD...
I HAVEN'T REPARTITIONNED MY DISK, because fdisk and minlabel aren't
compatible.... RH Install formatted swap space, root partition, and
installed the base system... I do not remember exactly , but I think I
made an error at the end with the boot manager install and install
exited...

But when I powercycled the system, and typed "b" or "BOOT -FL "i"
DKA000" the aboot starts... At the prompt I put 1/vmléinux.gz
root=/dev/sda2 .... (you can change the kernel with the one you want...
!!!)....

So here is what I made to get my Jensen working with RH4.2... I will try
with RH5.0 later, when I have the CD... If my chaotic text can help
somebody, it's good, if something isn't as described or wrong, or if you
have an addition e-mail me please.... Or better - reply to the
linux.redhat.axp  newsgroup or to the axp-list@redhat.com
mailing-list!!!

All files described on this text can be found on many ftp sites!!!

Thanx to all people in linux.redhat.axp ..... !!!

Peter Boutzev - Luxembourg
boutyev@usa.net










