You have a RH 5.0 system and made that symlink in the hopes of getting
RH 4.2 binaries to work? That won't fool rpm; it wants to know you
really installed a real libc.so.6.

And I don't see this discussed in the FAQ. I forget if people did
find a proper workaround to allow old binaries to run under RH 5.0.
It should be in the axp-archives.

BTW, you can query rpm to find out if it thinks that file is installed
with

rpm -q -f /lib/libc.so.6

-- g


