I'm guessing this is in my power table setup function. But it would be
best if recompile with -g and no optimization, and run it again in gdb.
Also watch out for warnings while compiling, if you have some header file
problem regarding any function that uses floating point you almost always
get SIGFPE since the compiler then assumes function arguments are
integers.

If you can't find the problem I can assist you in searching for your
problem (when I have some spare time).

