> 1. Is Firewire(IEEE 1394) really what the hype claims?

Yes and no. The transfer rate of the scsi bus is only one of many
bottlenecks. Firewire is a definite win if you have a good driver and
if you are trying to do intense I/O to more than one disk at once.
Bad drivers or only having one disk active will mean you won't see any
benefit.

The major winners are good external RAID systems plugged into good
adapters with good drivers. Even then it depends on usage; if you're
seek dominated, transfer isn't a bottleneck.

-- greg


