To: hurricane-list@redhat.com, Cristian Gafton <gafton@redhat.com>
Cc: J.S.Peatfield@damtp.cam.ac.uk
Subject: Re: glibc 2.0.7-6 and yp on alpha 
Resent-Date: 14 Apr 1998 16:14:12 -0000
Resent-From: hurricane-list@redhat.com
Resent-cc: recipient list not shown: ;

The following patch to ypbind-3.3 makes it work with glibc-2.0.7 on the alpha 
platform, I don't know yet if anything else has a different definition of 
binding stuff:

--cut-here--
--- rpcsvc/yp_prot.h.orig       Tue Apr 14 16:44:13 1998
+++ rpcsvc/yp_prot.h    Tue Apr 14 16:45:30 1998
@@ -247,7 +247,7 @@
 struct ypbind_resp {
        enum ypbind_resptype ypbind_status;
        union {
-               unsigned long ypbind_error;
+               u_int ypbind_error;
                struct ypbind_binding ypbind_bindinfo;
        } ypbind_respbody;
 };
--cut-here--

this definition is compatible with that in glibc.  Perhaps we really need to 
put these definitions only in one header file so we don't get this type of 
confusion when one is different...  I'll put the RPM/SRPM up if anyone want 
them...

Anyway yp is now working on alpha again!

 -- Jon


