I understand your problem (I'm the author of the glibc yp stuff). 
ypbind 3.3 isn't 64 bit clean, this was the reason why glibc prior 2.0.7pre
doesn't use the binding files. But that solution needs to much sockets. You 
could get the clean ypbind 3.3 sources  and my ypbind-3.3-glibc3.diff file
from ftp://ftp.kernel.org/pub/linux/utils/net/NIS/ .

This fixes the problem for Debian 2.0. Please try it out and tell me, if
it works for you, too.

There should be a FAQ entry in glibc about this problem, I will check if it is
in the current glibc 2.0.7 snapshot.

  Thorsten

