Procedure:

1. tell your ISP to change the mail exchange of domain
   onpurpose.com to point to your alpha server.

2. rpm -i sendmail-8.8.x-x.alpha.rpm

3. echo "onpurpose.com" >> /etc/sendmail.cw

4. /etc/rc.d/init.d/sendmail stop; /etc/rc.d/init.d/sendmail start

5. make sure "pop3 stream tcp ... ipop3d" is in /etc/inetd.conf
   uncommented.


That's it.
P.S. Nowadays spammers are everywhere, you probably want to
     investigate on how to prevent "mail relay" before you
     open up the smtp port.

