that attempts to use 'chattr' will not work.  Then ext2ed is your
recourse; using it you may manually clean affected inodes.

Backing up affected file system, reformatting **with check** affected 
drive, and restoring everything from a backup may be a more prudent
course of action on a longer run.  Skip your 'lost+found' when doing
a backup - of course.


