You would be benefitting yourself in the presetn and for the future by reading up on sendmail and learning some of its basics. That is the only way that you will be able to semi-control it. Furthermore, after doing some basic checking of your domain, you should have the Internic switch primary DNS to your box and have your ISP secondary from it (if that's what you want). Then you could change the MX records for your domain to point to the Alpha and then sendmail could be setup to deliver them wherever, be it the Alpha or some other box on your LAN.
Good luck,
