> What could be the problem?? I got a 164SX, 533Mhz system with
> Redhat5.0 Linux installed. The clock is running almost twice as
> fast as the CMOS clock. And the CMOS clock is running correctly.
>
> I have also tried the milo image from RH cdrom, it still has this
> problem. Any idea??

You don't need to re-compile Milo. Go to gatekeeper.dec.com
/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/milo-sx164-980324

Get that file and move it with the name "milo", replacing the original
"milo" file on the boot partition. Before, for safe, rename the original
milo to milo.old for example.

Regards,
Pablo Godel


