> 
> 	Also, What am I missing by not going with a 164LX - the cost
> is aprox. 2/3 more, and performance increase appears to be on the order
> of 15 - 20%?
> 

	The major differences are cache and available upgrade path.
(Yes, there are design differences as well, but it distills down 
pretty well to these two points)

-The 21164PC doesn't have the same cache configuration that the 21164a does.
-The SX doesn't have the same L3 cache as the LX.
-The LX will go to at least 600 MHz, the SX will most likely top out at 533.
(I've not seen any indication to the contrary on that point, any information
is welcome.)

Another difference that has nothing to do with design or performance, the
SX is intended to entice folks in the NT world away from the Pentium-II line.
I have all ideas that this contributes to the attractive pricing of the SX
line, but that's just an educated guess.  :-)

