> i'm running a pc164LX with rh5 and needed quota compiled into the kernel.
> I took the source i already had in /usr/src/linux and recompiled it with
> quota enabled.
> 
> i did a 'make mrproper'
> make clean; make dep
> make
> make boot
> make modules
> make module_install
> 
> then i rebooted but nothing ad changed. Is there a final step i'm missing?

Step 0: realize that the .config file distributed with the CD-ROM
doesn't correspond to the kernel you're using.

You have to "make config" and pick the right machine type, at the very
least. Note that make menuconfig and make xconfig are broken on the
alpha.

As the last step, you also have to copy
/usr/src/linux/arch/alpha/boot/vmlinux.gz to /. That's why nothing
changed. Had you done that it would have frozen at boot because
you've got the wrong machine type. Oh, and don't forget to
save your old kernel as /vmlinux.old.gz...

-- g


