Hugo van der Kooij wrote:
> And modules still don't work to well on Alpha.

I keep hearing that.  The only problems is that as far as I am
concerned modules **do work** on Alpha and I use them rather
heavily.  For example I set Alpha as a masquerading host well
over a year ago and this requires modules (only recently in
development kernels patches showed up patches which allow to lift
that requirement).

In the past there were problems with symbols and kerneld
was not operational but with current kernels (2.0.33 - to be
more precise) things mostly "just work".

Currently I am only aware about problems with a support for NFS
which cannot be compiled as a module.  The problem is that inlining
exports a "wrong" symbol and the right one is not available because
it is not inlined yet. :-(  Probably some kind of "wrapper" function
would be required.  Not really an Alpha issue.  It is possible that
some other module shows similar troubles.  I did not check all
of these which I needed (various file systems, including iso9660
and loopback, assorted ethernet cards, scsi tape, scsi "generic"
required by xcdroast, ide disks, ramdisk support, ....).

  Michal


