On Mon, 20 Apr 1998, Paul Mezzanini wrote:

> >You're doing something wrong.  I don't remember the exact proceedure (you
> I know, thats why i posted the msg :)

Well, the file /etc/rc.d/rc.sysinit holdes the quotas ...

You need /sbin/quotaon to be +x

Make sure you have "CONFIG_QUOTA=y" in /usr/src/linux/.config and be sure
that that is the proper running kernel.

Make sure you have 'usrquota' and/or 'grpquota' on your Options field in
/etc/fstab

And presuming you've 'touch'ed quota.user and quota.group with mode 600
that should be it ... make sure it's on the same filesystem with those
options in /etc/fstab ... dunno what else can be wrong.  Are you sure you
rebooted?  Or run the commands manually?

