in XFree86-3.3.1/xc/programs/Xserver/cfb32/cfb8segC.c there is a statement

    RROP_SOLID_MASK(( unsigned long *) addrp, e )

on my alpha addrp = PixelType * which equals a CARD32 * which equals to an
unsigned int *

UNFORTUNATELY, when u cast addrp to a long pointer, the macro RROP_SOLID_MASK,
will try to fetch
it as a long pointer ( ie get 8 bytes of a long value ). Thats ok, except that u
get an alignment fault when the address
doesn't point to an aligned long address, as it was in my case when the last
nibble of the addr was a 4.

i SUSPECT u want to keep the 32'ness of the addrp, and really don't want to go a
64 bit long pointer.

ergo use:
      RROP_SOLID_MASK(( unsigned int *) addrp, e )

or better yet, if u have the typedef:
   RROP_SOLID_MASK(( unsigned long32 *) addrp, e )
            or
   RROP_SOLID_MASK(( unsigned int32 *) addrp, e )




gat





