Deskstation seems to be somewhat behind times.  This used to work in
old days when there was an option to flash milo into NVRAM.  When milo
not present in NVRAM there is nothing which would keep your environment
variable from one cold boot to another (with a warm reboot "last used"
options should be remembered althouth I do not know yet if Ruffian board
has any quirks on its own; you are one of the first outside of an inner
circle who lay his/her hands on the thing :-).

> This, however, does not work.

On the other hand storing your boot command in OSLOADOPTIONS when
creating ARC/AlphaBIOS boot entry does work (or did until now).
This has a downside of a one command limit but this was not a very
big deal in practice.

> - If not, are the MILO messages logged in some file where I can
>   analyse them in more detail?

No, but scrolling back with Shift-PageUp (and Shift-PageDown) should
work already.

A hint: typing 'show dev' at milo prompt will get you only a bunch of
messages from milo not mixed with a similar ones from a kernel you boot.
You type your boot command later, when you will get your MILO> prompt
back.  Boot messages from a kernel can be replayed with 'dmesg'
command and are stored in /var/log/dmesg file.

  Michal


