Gary,

Dustin's original note did not specify who manufactured his 875 card, and he 
was using the ncr53c,7xx driver.  I suggested that he try the ncr53c8xx driver, 
which is definitely the right driver to use for IntraServer 875 cards.  I'm not 
sure what cards use the c7xx driver.

If you have the *same* problem, then perhaps you also are using the c7xx driver 
rather than c8xx.  The c7xx driver will *not* run IntraServer cards.  I'm not 
sure what combinations of "make" cause the ncr53c8xx driver to appear.  Another 
post suggests that using either "make xconfig" or "make menuconfig" is a bad 
idea.  I've also heard that if you respond with 'y' to the ncr53c,7xx driver, 
then prompts for the ncr53c8xx driver will not appear.  However if you compile 
with "make config", and specify 'N' for all ncr related drivers, you will be 
prompted for the ncr53c8xx.  This is the driver to use for IntraServer cards, 
and to the best of my knowledge for all 875 based cards.

hope this helps.

cheers,
Kevin

