   I had a similar problem, where the system would boot from MILO to the
linux kernel, and when Linux went to initialize the SCSI card it would
stop. 
  My cure: I read in a FAQ somewhere that you should upgrade your NCR
drivers in your 2.0.33 kernel. I am currently running 
NCR53c8xx - revision 2.4c drivers, 
which I believe were the recomended drivers for a stable
system, but missing some features of the newer drivers. the filename of
the patch you want is something like ncr53c8xx-?.??-to-?.??.patch.gz. Find
out what version you have now in your linux/drivers/scsi/ncr53c8xx.c . You
may need to apply multiple patches to your kernel to get to the version
you want.

  For a new FAQ/info, I think you can find more info at:
ftp://ftp.wauug.org/pub/roudier
   (found in the linux/drivers/scsi/README-ncr53c8xx file)

