I wonder if anyone who is running XF86_SVGA ver 3.3.2 with Matrox Millenium
is seeing the problem I have.

My machine is PC164, Redhat 5.0 for alpha, kernel 2.1.90.

With netscape communicator 4, either running locally or from a remote
client, if one drag the little icon between  the label <Bookmarks> and 
<Location> on the Location Toolbar, the screen goes blank immediately.
There is no way to recover the screen except to reboot.

Using gdb on the X server reveals that it is busy looping in:

#0  0x1200c64a0 in xf86ReadSparse8 ()
#1  0x120045a70 in MGAStormSync ()
#2  0x12004190c in cfbCopyPlane32to1 ()
#3  0x120076af8 in vgaEnterLeaveVT ()
#4  0x12011bab8 in GiveUp ()
(gdb) 

I guess the graphics hardware is set into a seriously confused state by a
previous operation. There is no way to recover other than reset the
hardware by rebooting the machine. It is only the graphics card that is
affected, everything else on the machine is normal.

Ver 3.3.1 copes with the same action perfectly fine.


Regards,

Sai-Lai Lo


