On Sun, 12 Apr 1998, Peter Boutzev wrote:

> Finally my Jensen boots using aboot... But the problems are not finished
[...]
> I tried to re minlabel the disk, and minilabel didn't see the partitions
> I made with Disk Druid at RH Install... I think that Disk Druid isn't
> the right prog to partition HDs on Jensens, but I am not sure...
> But the minlabel partitions seem not to be working (mkfs.ext2 halts on
> them)....

 For Alphas starting from SRM you may find the generic `fdisk' useful.
Just select <b> ("edit bsd disklabel") upon startup and make sure you have
some space for booting purposes reserved at the beginning (just as you
mentioned).  When you have your system installed you will be able to
perform `swriteboot' to make your system start off the hard disk.
`Minlabel' is really crude and `fdisk' has an additional advantage of
being called directly from Red Hat's installer -- you don't need to
perform any dirty tricks during the installation.

