With regards to your message at 05:34 PM 04-23-98 -0400, Todd Fleisher.
Where you stated:
>Hello,
>	Can anyone tell me how to get milo to remember where I boot Linux from?
Right now, when I reboot the system it will remember the location but waits
30seconds before booting. However, when I power off the system it just
boots up to the milo prompt and sits there.
>Thanks,
>Todd
This depends slightly on which firmware (ARC or AlphaBIOS) you have, but
the concept remains the same in either case. There are environmental values
you can set for passing parameters to milo. Often there is a default, such
as "no debug" or similar. Merely replace this with your boot parameters,
such as "b sda2:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda2" or similar. Obviously the actual
devices and partitions will depend on your disk setup..





