Hello,

Anyone out there able to use the ftape driver (in any incarnation) on
his/her Alpha box? No luck on my XLT300 :-( The ancient version in kernel
2.0.33 does not compile. The new 3.04 version compiles fine as a module but
is not able to detect the fdc. Normal floppy access works fine. The drive
works fine on my intel box.

Some things I found/tried:

 - The detection code for the kernel floppy driver is more or less the same
as the one in the ftape driver but the kernel names the fdc PC87306 while
the same check in the ftape driver names the fdc PC8744 which is assumed to
be i82077A compatible. Does not seem to be a problem.

- /proc/ioports and /proc/dma do not list the floppy device. It works fine but
it does not show up. Weird....

- after a reboot ftape detects the fdc as a pre 1991 i8272 which is not good
(very different part in the detection code)

- after unloading and reloading once (or more) no fdc at all is found by
ftape


Any suggestions ?

Thanks -- Jaap

