I suspect you need to turn on loop device, RAM disk and initial
RAM disk support.

From my .config:

#
# Additional Block Devices
#
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_LOOP=y  <---
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_MD=y
CONFIG_MD_LINEAR=m
CONFIG_MD_STRIPED=m
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_RAM=y  <---
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_INITRD=y  <---

This is alluded to in the RedHat manual, although they would have to
work really hard to make it more confusing.

Would also be nice if RedHat distributed the /usr/src/linux/.config 
file they used to build the kernel on the distribution CD.
Then we would not have to play .config roulette trying to figure out
which options are really needed.

