Murray Stokely wrote:
> 
> How can you then get MILO to automatically boot a kernel instead of
> waiting for the user to enter something like ..
> 
> 'boot sda5:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda5'
> 
> ?

	IN ARC or ALPHABIOS, there is a line called 'osloadoptions' which is
located in the screen where you setup your boot selections (IE: NT4.0,
Linux, etc).

	IN the osloadoptions field, enter in your boot string, and it will get
passed to MILO at startup. MILO will then execute the passed string
without pausing.

	Hope that helps..





