Hi!

I just would like to point out that there is a new revision of my
optimized encoder for encoding layer 3 mpeg audio. And now it even has a
revision number! :)

This version has a bug-fix which affected (to my knowledge) FreeBSD and
non glibc2 versions of alpha linux. In my pow_nint_table I calculated one
value too much which led to an imaginary result. I never used this result
anywhere, but on some systems the encoder crashed with an arithmetic trap.
Thanks to Joakim Roubert <jokke@df.lth.se> for pointing the problem out.

Also included in this version is a nice 10% speed up due to some simple
code inlining. Your mileage may vary, this was measured on my SX164.

In this process (and after seeing the amount of people that was
interrested in my work) I have also moved the archive to a more
informative place. This is the new URL:

ftp://wopr.campus.luth.se/pub/mpeg_layer_3/encoder1.0.tgz

New versions will have different version numbers.

/Andreas


