I've been struggling for a week to get my Digital AlphaServer
1000 4/266 to install linux.

The manual for 5.0 says that it is a "Mikasa" class machine. I
searched the 5.0 CD for a mikasa kernel image to no avail. I then
read the newsgroups and searched extensively on Altavista, and found
that some people had installed with the images found on the DEC
FTP site.

I downloaded the kernel and ramdisk images from there and was
able to boot the floppy, but it hung after mounting /dev/fd0
and loading the ramdisk image.

I finally went to the RedHat site and found, a file called
mikasa-s.img in the RH *4.2* distribution.

I made a rawrite disk from my Windows box and it booted and installed
RH 5.0 just fine! I booted the floppy from the SRM console.

