Hi,
I have put our mikasa kernel (2.0.33) with a milo, milo.dd and linload.exe on
ftp://ftp.island.net/pub/Linux/Linux-alpha/

You can dd the milo.dd to a floppy, copy the vmlinux.gz to a floppy, and
then boot the milo floppy from srm (boot dva0)

from milo do
boot fd0:/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda1 (or your root partition).

Once booted put the vmlinux.gz in / or /boot milo and linload.exe on a 2M
dos partition.

Setup for the ARC console is at
http://www.redhat.com/support/docs/rhl/manual/manual/doc107.html

and setting the OSLOADOPTIONS in the ARC boot setup to 
boot sda1:/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda1

so that the ARC will send milo the boot flags it need.

Hope that helps,
