Maybe you'd like to have a look at http://www.axene.com They have various
office applications available for several flavors of Linux. The
wordprocessor "XAllWrite" is currently in beta.

I've emailed axene (contact@axene.com) asking for a Linux/Alpha version. 
While they don't have a Linux/Alpha version right now, they answered that
they are planning to provide Linux/Alpha binaries "within a few weeks".
They are also planning to support _all_ Linux ports.

Pricing is IMHO rather moderate, but from what I've seen their apps don't
have all the bells and whistles that big programs like Staroffice or
Applixware have. (Actually, it reminded me more of the various *Works
packages). OTOH the apps looked rather snappy (even when I was testing one
of them on a 60MHz Pentium) and seem to be fine for small documents that
don't need all the bells and whistles anyway.

They also have a DTP Software available, BTW...

Maybe sending email to contact@axene.com asking for a Linux/Alpha version
could speed up the process of creating Linux/Alpha binaries of their
apps... ;-) 

