Fine, redo the config.  Select N for use Digital Code.  Recompile.  Hrm.
Compile errors in x86_sysenv.c.  Move the loops_per_sec and malloc declarations
to just above the #ifdef MINI_DIGITAL_BIOSEMU line.  Success!  Compiles and
produces lots of milo.  Copy to floppy.  Boot?  Not a chance.  Hangs at swapping
to PALCode (again, sigh).

Hardware configuration:  PC164LX board, 512MB ram, Buslogic BT-958 SCSI Card,
