On Thu, 23 Apr 1998, Edwin Koshimoto wrote:

> This is very puzzling to me.  The Postgresql folks have told me that
> they don't have the resources to debug this so it's upon the linux
> alpha community.  It seemed like the Digital Unix folks have got the
> problem solved on their end.  6.3.2 seems to have this same
> problem on my RH 5.0 PC164 machine. I thought 6.3.2 was supposed to
> fix this on all alphas???

	6.3.2 was supposed to partialy fix Linux/Alpha. I was the one who
did the patches for 6.3.2 for Linux/Alpha. They allow me on my UDB running
RH4.0 to compile pgsql successfully, and run initdb with no problems. It
is not totally fixed on Linux/Alpha yet, as there are still some 64 bit
issues to sort out on the datatype at least (regression tests are still
failing on datetime among others). 

> I've been told to look for old libraries but I can't find any.  Well,
> hopefully somebody can set me straight!

	It looks like the new glibc library that RH5.0 uses is breaking
things that were not broken before. I don't know how much success there
has been had with running pgsql on RH5.0 Intel, but if it is working for
them, then that improves the chances that it will work on Alpha, right? I
don't have any RH5.0 machines, so I am afraid I can't help on this point. 
	Either way, if even with 6.3.2 pgsql (and the alpha patches) is
still not working, then the problem is beyond any that have been hit
so far. I would probably point my finger at the glibc version that RH5.0
uses. I guess we need some brave soul to dig around and see if they can
determine where the incompatiblity is occuring. 
	This probably doesn't set things straight, but hopefully it at
least sheds some light on them. TTYL.

