On Sun, 26 Apr 1998, Todd Fleisher wrote:

> 	After recompiling my kernel, I get the following error when trying to fire up my X display:
> 	Fatal server error:
> 	(--) DEC_TGA: MemBase needed for TGA support - check /proc/pci for base 	address.
> 
> Can anyone enlighten me to the cause and fix for this?

Uhm, pretty much everything you need to know is right here; the cause was
that you recompiled your kernel.  You don't say to/from what, but
evidently things changed between 2.0.x and 2.1.x if that's what you did.

The fix is to "cat /proc/pci" and look for the line that says TGA.
Somewhere there is a memory base address and you need to put this address
in your XF86Config file, under the heading MemBase.

