Use the one most appropriate for your system.  If you are compilimg
2.0.30, get 2.0.30-0.4.gz; If you are compiling 2.0.32 or newer, get
3.0.32-0.1.gz. 

> I am using RH5.0(2.0.30) on my Alpha 233MHz machine.

I would recommend, uhm, probably waiting, actually.  I hear there are
problems with 2.0.33 on alpha (though my machine has been up a couple
weeks with no apparent problems) and 2.0.34 should be out before long.
However, if you're in a rush, grab 2.0.33 and the patches for 2.0.32.

> By the way, is there any FAQ that can tell me how to use these patches?

I dunno ... it's probably expected that you know.  However, you're going
to want to do something like the following:

# cd /usr/src
# mv linux linux-stock-redhat
# tar xf (path/to/kernel-2.0.33.tar.gz)
# cd linux
# zcat (or "gunzip -c") (path/to/patches-2.0.33.gz) | patch -p1
# make config

In my experience, 'make menuconfig' is utterly broken, and 'make xconfig'
will work, but only the first time you use it - YMMV.

