I looked at the .c file you have at this link and the problem seems pretty
simple.  Maybe that's why nobody answered, or maybe everyone's working on
the Netscape code.  Anyhow, on pages 11 and 13 (of 22 - you do the math)
you have two fopen calls, each opening the file in "a+" mode.  In this
mode, fseek()s will work and you can read data from any position, but all
data written will ALWAYS be written to the end of the file.  This is
'append' mode and was created specifically for logging facilities.  You
want to use mode "w+" (read/write) and don't worry, it won't destroy your
ouput file like the plain old "w"-mode.

