	I have found that the best way to go about instaling RedHat on the UDB is as follows:
  1) Make your bootdisk from the redhat-4.2 set (noname)
  2) Make your ramdisk from the redhat-5.0 set (ramdisk.img)
	The bootdisk that is distributed with redhat-5.0 includes the tulip.c ethernet driver which doesn't work on the UDB. Hence, trying an FTP/NFS install with the wrong kernel will not work. Furthermore, when the system copies the kernel from the bootdisk, your system will not support ethernet.
	As for kernel versions, I am running 2.0.30 without problem (knock wood). Furthermore, I have been unable to compile a good 2.0.33 kernel.

Regards,
Todd

