On Mon, 27 Apr 1998, Tony Galan wrote:

> Can anyone help me with this problem?
> I tried to start X on my UDB , but got an error instead.
> The error reads:
> 
> Fatal server error:
> (--) DEC_TGA: MemBase needed for TGA Support - check /proc/pci for base
> address.
> 
> What should I do to get X up?

cat /proc/pci

note memory base for the DEC TGA, it's something like 0x?000000.

Edit your /etc/X11/XF86Config, add this line in the Card description.

MemBase 0x?000000

This is definitely FAQ and I think is in the RedHat manual, check the
webpages and support maillist archives.

Greg


