> d.teTeX/teTeX-0.9/texk/xdvik/xdvi.c:1343: undefined reference to `XOpenDisplay'
> d.teTeX/teTeX-0.9/texk/xdvik/xdvi.c:1350: undefined reference to `XGetDefault'

As all these functions are provided by a basic libX11, not even one of
extra toolkits,  it is obvious that you are not linking this library.
Why it is hard to tell as you are telling what you are doing and my
crystal ball is in a storage.  Probably xdvi came with Imakefile and you
did not bother to run 'xmkmf -a' before trying to compile but instead
you are using Makefile which happened to be siting there and which was
for a totally different system.  This has really nothing to do with
Linux and even less with Alpha.

In case of sources with no Imakefile around it is often advantageous,
instead of hacking Makefile and forgetting something, to provide
a link 'ln -s X11R6 X11' in /usr.  It is harmless until the moment
when you replace your revision of X with the next one.  Not for a some
time yet.

  Michal


