On Sun, 26 Apr 1998, Keith Baker wrote:

> How would I got about remote booting a multia...  the ROM seems to have
> the intelegance...  I have an NFS disk availiable to hold the root
> partition...  Which console should I use and how do I switch?  (ARC
> (probably not),OpenVMS,DU (I think))...  Other than that I am kinda
> clueless...  Thanks...

 From SRM you may issue `boot ewa0' (or any other Ether device).  There is
a bunch of console variables which control the behaviour of this command. 
They are easy to figure out (they are undocumented in the manual; at least
in mine) as they contain the "bootp" or "tftp" string.  Note that the
retry counts are -signed- integers (it hit me when I set one of them to
"ffffffff"). 

 There is a target in the makefile of the 'aboot' package that creates a
net-bootable kernel image.  There is one in the 2.1 distribution of Linux
kernel, too.  Haven't tested any of these though.

 BTW, I am speaking of AlphaServers but it should not matter as the SRM
consoles are compatible from user's point of view.

