Stefan Boresch writes:
> 
> Can anyone shed some light on this puzzle? What exactly does the
> portmap rpm break? The code to set the clock in rc.sysinit works OK if
> executed separately after the boot process,

In that case the simple workaround is to set clock once again at
the end of your boot process in rc.local.  True, whatever was
written to logfiles, between portmap buggered your clock and you
restored it back, will have a weird time-stamp - which is annoying -
but at least this will preserve your sanity until you will have the
problem licked.

The more radical intervention is to edit a portmap startup script
and fix clock there.

  Michal


