Uncle George wrote:

> what do u do for backup storage ? 9 gigs is a whole lot of real estate.
>

That's relatively small actually. I'm sure others on the list use lots of disk too but I use
150GB spread across 10 systems. (not just Alphas) In my case it's mostly for handling
temporary files generated by my SW. It's easy to have 2-3GB consumed on each
system by one parallel application and if you're lazy like me, you clean up only when
you need to. Any data that is important came off a tape anyway so backups aren't
needed. Course the output is important but it's relatively small when things are done.
On the order of 2GB. or so. I think news/mail servers consume huge amounts of
disk and would need backing up.... I use an Exabyte 7GB Eliant 820, about 1.0-1.5
MB/sec. There are faster tape drives but they are $$. If I had to get a faster one,
it would be the new Sony AIT 8mm or a DLT 7000. I can buy a whole Alpha system
for the price of one of those drives!!
Customers I work with use mainframe class tape drives on their UNIX systems, STK
Timberlines, IBM 3590, attached to large tape silo conplexes (6000 cartridges each, can be
interconnected. Largest I've seen was 24 silos for 144000 tapes near line!)

My $.02....

Wes

