I recently tried to use an Adaptec 4 port network card as was never successful. 
So you can't just put any pci card in that works on intel/linux.  It seems that
milo has a hand in finding or placing the card in memory and the Adaptec/Cogent
card was not properly recognized by milo.  Also if you are
experienced with Redhat for intel dont expect to change over to an Alpha and
not experience a learning curve.  The kernel RedHat ships is not modular so you
may want to spend some time re-compiling.  I would suggest putting 2.0.33 on
and if you are using tulip based network cards then you should get the latest
tulip.c file and cp it into linux/drivers/net.  The older driver works but the
newer one has some nice features.  


