Minor nit:

The definition of size_t is the type that sizeof returns, and is an
unsigned integral type. There is no mention if the pointer size in the
definition of size_t in the C standard that I have in front of me.

The definition if ptrdiff_t is the signed integral type returned by the
subtraction of two pointers.

That is not to say that the "#define size_t unsigned int" is correct.
It probably is not. Anyhow, the canonical definition is in <stddef.h>


