>	So, what's a simple explanation for why someone woudl do that?  
>Lack of understanding?  Some optimization tradeoff?

Usually a combination of:

  -  Lack of understanding of the issues

  -  Lack of faith that the software will have much longevity

  -  Belief that the underlying system is the One True System everyone
     should, and probably will be someday, using, anyway

  -  Assumption that the way other code they're looking at does
     something must therefore be "right", sometimes without realizing
     that the other code's containing application is inherently
     non-portable while theirs isn't

  -  Lack of time to "do it right" *and* later "make it fast" such
     that it remains portable

Etc.
