>>> "Maciej W. Rozycki" said:
> 
>  I am not sure whether `fdisk' in BSD mode calls the 'ioctl' to inform the
> kernel that the geometry of partitions changed (it calls it when in PC
> mode).  If your kernel doesn't output something like:
> 
> Partition check:
>  sda: sda1 sda2 sda3
> 
> then `fdisk' does not perform the necessary step.  You have to perform it
> manually.  The simpliest, though an ugly way is just to reboot the
> machine.

Actually, fdisk *does* make the correct ioctl to update the kernel's version
of the partition tables. I found this out when using "minlabel" which does
NOT make the correct ioctl call (or perhaps none). After finishing up with
minlabel, I simply enter into fdisk's BSD option and tell it to write the
label and exit. Works like a charm, for me, anyway... ;-}

