Hi folks,
  I had "pliped" Alpha/Linux on AlphaServer 800 for a few month
w/o major problems. There is only problem with timeouts and spare
PLIP lockups - both can be resolved with 'rmmod plip;insmod plip' 
(for example from cron). I'm using following scripts on Linux/Alpha
(Replace Internet address with yours...)

---- PLIP Alpha client side:
---- plipup
#!/bin/sh
# 147.231.75.76 - Alpha Linux
# 147.231.75.56 - PLIP router connected to ethernet - Linux/i386
rmmod lp
insmod plip io=0x3bc irq=7
ifconfig plip0 147.231.75.76 pointopoint \
147.231.75.56 mtu 570 netmask 255.255.255.0 -arp up
/sbin/route add 147.231.75.56 plip0             #NOTE: don't add whole net
/sbin/route add default gw 147.231.75.56 plip0  # it is contained in 
                                                # default target...
---------------------------------------------
--- plipdown ---
#!/bin/sh
ifconfig plip0 down
---------------------------------------------


PLIP server (router to ethernet) scripts:
----- plipup
#!/bin/sh
rmmod lp
RHOST=147.231.75.76
ifconfig plip1  147.231.75.56 pointopoint $RHOST\
    netmask 255.255.255.0 mtu 570 -arp up
route add -host $RHOST  plip1
arp -s $RHOST 00:A0:24:75:97:6E pub
---- plipdown
#!/bin/sh
ifconfig plip1 down
---------------

Good Luck!

             Henryk Paluch, paluch@terezka.ufa.cas.cz




