> Apr 29 21:23:37 octavia kernel: Detected scsi disk sdb at scsi0, channel 0, id 2, lun 0
> Apr 29 21:23:37 octavia kernel: scsi0 : target 4 accepting asynchronous SCSI
> Apr 29 21:23:37 octavia kernel: scsi0 : setting target 4 to asynchronous SCSI
> Apr 29 21:23:37 octavia kernel:   Vendor: DEC       Model: RRD43   (C) DEC   Rev: 1084
> Apr 29 21:23:37 octavia kernel:   Type:   CD-ROM                             ANSI SCSI revision: 02
> Apr 29 21:23:37 octavia kernel: Detected scsi CD-ROM sr0 at scsi0, channel 0, id 4, lun 0
> Apr 29 21:23:37 octavia kernel: scsi : detected 1 SCSI cdrom 2 SCSI disks total.
> Apr 29 21:23:37 octavia kernel: SCSI device sda: hdwr sector= 512 bytes. Sectors= 2110812 [1030 MB] [1.0 GB]
> Apr 29 21:23:37 octavia kernel: SCSI device sdb: hdwr sector= 512 bytes. Sectors= 2061108 [1006 MB] [1.0 GB]
> 
> (from /var/log/messages)
> 

cdda2wav uses the SCSI generic interface.
SCSI devices are assigned to /dev/sg[abc...] in the order that they are 
detected, so in your case id 0 is /dev/sga, id 2 is /dev/sgb and id 4
(your CD-ROM drive) is /dev/sgc.

Before you added the 2nd SCSI disk the CD-ROM was probably /dev/sgb.

You can tell cdda2wav which SCSI generic device to use
either by compiling in a default or thru a command line argument.

