> $(shell $(AS) --version >& ./GAS_VER)

This is wrong syntax.  If you call bash under a name /bin/sh, like
Makefile does, you cannot use any bash extensions.  The line should
read:

$(shell $(AS) --version > ./GAS_VER 2>&1)

and redirects both stderr and stdout to ./GAS_VER.  Your "fix"
just left stderr alone.

  Michal


