fine, but I'm unable to boot the install kernel. I've tried the avanti.img
and avanti-s.img from both RedHat 4.2 and 5.0 but I get the same results.
I've tried booting the kernel from MILO, and also directly from the SRM
console. 

In both cases I'm told that the kernel is loading, and I see the floppy
drive being accessed for a bit. Then I get a message indicating that we're
switching to the kernel, and nothing else happens.

From the SRM console I do:

  boot dva0 -file vmlinux.gz -flags "load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1"

Things seem to be looking good, and then I see:

  aboot: loading compressed vmlinux.gz...  (I see the floppy working)
  aboot: ok, now starting the kernel...

And then it just sits there :) From my MILO boot floppy, I type:

  boot fd0:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1

Again, I get some pretty reasonable looking messages, ending with:

  Bootstrap complete, kernel @ 0xfffffc0000310000, sp @ 0xfffffc0000304000
  ...turning on virtual addressing and jumping to the Linux Kernel

Then my cursor sits there flashing and that's all she wrote.

I'd really appreciate any ideas you have. Like I said, I've tried 4
different kernel images with the same results. 


Thanks,

Rich

